[{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"예쁘다","english":"pretty; beautiful","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-07"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["예뻐요","it is pretty","ㅡ drops before 어"],["예쁜 가방","a pretty bag","noun-modifier form"],["꽃이 예뻐요","the flowers are pretty","with 이/가"],["예쁜 옷을 샀어요","I bought pretty clothes","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["이 가방이 정말 예뻐요.","This bag is really pretty.","요-form ending"],["예쁜 신발을 사고 싶어요.","I want to buy pretty shoes.","modifier form 예쁜"],["동생이 예쁜 모자를 썼어요.","My sibling wore a pretty hat.","modifier in object"]],"nuance":"예쁘다 means pretty or lovely, often for things, people, or scenery. The ㅡ drops before 어요, giving 예뻐요.","mistakes":["Saying 예쁘어요 instead of 예뻐요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"멋있다","english":"cool; stylish","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-07"],"grammarIds":["grammar-modifier-nl","grammar-particle-i-ga"],"usage":[["멋있어요","it is cool","regular 있다 ending"],["멋있는 사람","a cool person","있다 takes 는"],["옷이 멋있어요","the clothes are stylish","with 이/가"],["멋있는 차를 봤어요","I saw a cool car","modifier 멋있는"]],"examples":[["그 배우가 정말 멋있어요.","That actor is really cool.","요-form 멋있어요"],["멋있는 옷을 입고 싶어요.","I want to wear stylish clothes.","modifier 멋있는"],["오빠가 멋있는 시계를 샀어요.","My older brother bought a cool watch.","modifier before noun"]],"nuance":"멋있다 describes someone or something stylish or impressive. Because it ends in 있다, the modifier form is 멋있는, not 멋있은.","mistakes":["Using 멋있은 instead of 멋있는"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"길다","english":"long","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["길어요","it is long","regular 요-form"],["긴 머리","long hair","ㄹ drops before ㄴ"],["길이 길어요","the road is long","with 이/가"],["긴 다리를 건너요","I cross a long bridge","modifier 긴"]],"examples":[["이 길이 너무 길어요.","This road is too long.","요-form 길어요"],["긴 치마를 입었어요.","I wore a long skirt.","modifier 긴, ㄹ drop"],["머리가 길어서 잘랐어요.","My hair was long so I cut it.","요-form before 서"]],"nuance":"길다 means long in length or time. Before the modifier ㄴ, the final ㄹ drops, so the modifier form is 긴, not 길은.","mistakes":["Saying 길은 머리 instead of 긴 머리"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"짧다","english":"short","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["짧아요","it is short","ㅏ vowel takes 아요"],["짧은 치마","a short skirt","modifier 짧은"],["다리가 짧아요","the legs are short","with 이/가"],["짧은 머리가 좋아요","I like short hair","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["이 바지가 좀 짧아요.","These pants are a bit short.","요-form 짧아요"],["짧은 글을 썼어요.","I wrote a short text.","modifier 짧은"],["방학이 짧아서 아쉬워요.","The vacation is short so I am sad.","요-form before 서"]],"nuance":"짧다 means short and is the opposite of 길다. The stem vowel ㅏ takes 아요, and the modifier form is 짧은.","mistakes":["Saying 짧어요 instead of 짧아요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"빠르다","english":"fast; quick","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["빨라요","it is fast","르 irregular form"],["빠른 차","a fast car","modifier 빠른"],["기차가 빨라요","the train is fast","with 이/가"],["빠른 길로 가요","I go the fast way","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["이 기차가 정말 빨라요.","This train is really fast.","르 irregular 빨라요"],["빠른 답장을 받았어요.","I got a quick reply.","modifier 빠른"],["인터넷이 빨라서 좋아요.","The internet is fast so I like it.","르 irregular before 서"]],"nuance":"빠르다 means fast and follows the 르 irregular, so 르 becomes ㄹㄹ before 아요, giving 빨라요. The modifier form 빠른 is regular.","mistakes":["Saying 빠라요 or 빠르어요 instead of 빨라요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"높다","english":"high; tall","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-modifier-nl","grammar-particle-i-ga"],"usage":[["높아요","it is high","ㅗ vowel takes 아요"],["높은 산","a high mountain","modifier 높은"],["건물이 높아요","the building is tall","with 이/가"],["높은 곳에 올라가요","I go up to a high place","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["저 산이 아주 높아요.","That mountain is very high.","요-form 높아요"],["높은 빌딩을 봤어요.","I saw a tall building.","modifier 높은"],["가격이 높아서 안 샀어요.","The price was high so I did not buy it.","요-form before 서"]],"nuance":"높다 means high or tall and is used for mountains, buildings, and prices. The stem vowel ㅗ takes 아요, giving 높아요.","mistakes":["Saying 높어요 instead of 높아요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"멀다","english":"far","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["멀어요","it is far","regular 요-form"],["먼 곳","a far place","ㄹ drops before ㄴ"],["학교가 멀어요","the school is far","with 이/가"],["먼 길을 걸어요","I walk a long way","modifier 먼"]],"examples":[["집이 회사에서 멀어요.","My home is far from work.","요-form 멀어요"],["먼 나라로 여행 가요.","I travel to a far country.","modifier 먼, ㄹ drop"],["역이 멀어서 버스를 타요.","The station is far so I take the bus.","요-form before 서"]],"nuance":"멀다 means far in distance. Before the modifier ㄴ, the final ㄹ drops, so the modifier form is 먼, not 멀은.","mistakes":["Saying 멀은 곳 instead of 먼 곳"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"가깝다","english":"close; near","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["가까워요","it is close","ㅂ irregular form"],["가까운 곳","a close place","modifier 가까운"],["집이 가까워요","the house is near","with 이/가"],["가까운 가게에 가요","I go to a nearby store","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["지하철역이 가까워요.","The subway station is close.","ㅂ irregular 가까워요"],["가까운 친구를 만났어요.","I met a close friend.","modifier 가까운"],["회사가 가까워서 걸어가요.","Work is close so I walk.","ㅂ irregular before 서"]],"nuance":"가깝다 means close or near and is the opposite of 멀다. It follows the ㅂ irregular, so ㅂ becomes 우, giving 가까워요 and 가까운.","mistakes":["Saying 가깝아요 instead of 가까워요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"깨끗하다","english":"clean","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-06"],"grammarIds":["grammar-modifier-nl","grammar-particle-i-ga"],"usage":[["깨끗해요","it is clean","하다 becomes 해요"],["깨끗한 방","a clean room","modifier 깨끗한"],["방이 깨끗해요","the room is clean","with 이/가"],["깨끗한 옷을 입어요","I wear clean clothes","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["이 화장실이 깨끗해요.","This bathroom is clean.","하다 form 깨끗해요"],["깨끗한 물을 마셔요.","I drink clean water.","modifier 깨끗한"],["방이 깨끗해서 기분이 좋아요.","The room is clean so I feel good.","하다 form before 서"]],"nuance":"깨끗하다 means clean and follows the regular 하다 pattern, becoming 깨끗해요. The modifier form is 깨끗한.","mistakes":["Saying 깨끗하요 instead of 깨끗해요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"무겁다","english":"heavy","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-07"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["무거워요","it is heavy","ㅂ irregular form"],["무거운 가방","a heavy bag","modifier 무거운"],["짐이 무거워요","the luggage is heavy","with 이/가"],["무거운 짐을 들어요","I carry heavy luggage","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["이 가방이 너무 무거워요.","This bag is too heavy.","ㅂ irregular 무거워요"],["무거운 상자를 옮겼어요.","I moved a heavy box.","modifier 무거운"],["가방이 무거워서 힘들어요.","The bag is heavy so it is hard.","ㅂ irregular before 서"]],"nuance":"무겁다 means heavy and follows the ㅂ irregular, so ㅂ becomes 우, giving 무거워요 and 무거운.","mistakes":["Saying 무겁어요 instead of 무거워요"]},
{"kind":"adjective","hangul":"가볍다","english":"light (in weight)","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-07"],"grammarIds":["grammar-irregular-stems","grammar-modifier-nl"],"usage":[["가벼워요","it is light","ㅂ irregular form"],["가벼운 노트북","a light laptop","modifier 가벼운"],["가방이 가벼워요","the bag is light","with 이/가"],["가벼운 옷을 입어요","I wear light clothes","modifier before noun"]],"examples":[["이 노트북이 정말 가벼워요.","This laptop is really light.","ㅂ irregular 가벼워요"],["가벼운 가방을 샀어요.","I bought a light bag.","modifier 가벼운"],["짐이 가벼워서 편해요.","The luggage is light so it is comfortable.","ㅂ irregular before 서"]],"nuance":"가볍다 means light in weight and is the opposite of 무겁다. It follows the ㅂ irregular, giving 가벼워요 and 가벼운.","mistakes":["Saying 가볍어요 instead of 가벼워요"]},
